<title>FRANCE: AI(R) shortlists engine firms for new jet family.</title>
<headline>AI(R) shortlists engine firms for new jet family.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>European aircraft consortium Aero International (Regional) (AI(R) said on Wednesday that it has shortlisted engines from General Electric and SNECMA/Pratt &amp; Whitney for its planned AI(R) 70 family of regional jets.</p>
<p>AI(R), which groups France's Aerospatiale, British Aerospace Plc and Alenia of Italy's Finmeccanica, has shortlisted GE's CF 34-8C and the SPW 14 from SNECMA and Pratt &amp; Whitney as candidates for the jet, which is due to become operational in 1997. A decision is due next spring. P&amp;W is a United Technologies Corp.</p>
</text>
